    <section anchor="the-function">
      <name>The Function</name>
      <blockquote anchor="R-SHA1-OUT">
        <t>The SHA-1 algorithm produces a 160-bit message digest for a * given data stream that can serve as a means of providing a * "fingerprint" for a message.
<xref section="8.2.1" sectionFormat="of" target="RFC6234"/></t>
      </blockquote>
    </section>
    <section anchor="the-test-driver">
      <name>The Test Driver</name>
      <blockquote anchor="R-DRIVER">
        <t>The following code is a main program test driver to exercise the code in sha1.c, sha224-256.c, sha384-512.c, hmac.c, and hkdf.c.
<xref section="8.5" sectionFormat="of" target="RFC6234"/></t>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote anchor="R-ASCII">
        <t>Note that the tests assume that character values are as in [US-ASCII] and a run time check warns if the code appears to have been compiled with some other character system.
<xref section="8.5" sectionFormat="of" target="RFC6234"/></t>
      </blockquote>
    </section>
